# Check a stretch of planned motion against the obstacle grid: how long must each segment
# take, given what's around the robot now? Answered by stretch_obstacle_grid's
# obstacle_monitor_node.
#
# Joints use the driver's command names (as in PlanJointTrajectory). The first point is where
# the motion starts, usually the robot's current state. Joints a trajectory leaves out are
# filled in from /joint_states. mobile_base_rotation_joint is relative to the base's heading
# when the request is sent. Points may be far apart: the node checks in steps of the
# planner's check_resolution and adds the results up per segment.
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory trajectory
---
bool success
string message

# Per segment (between consecutive points), from the slowest step within it:
# min_duration: the segment may take no less than this (s). Its planned time is
#   time_from_start[i + 1] - time_from_start[i]; anything shorter must be slowed down.
float32[] min_duration
# Speed allowed at the limiting piece of the robot (m/s), and the shape it belongs to.
float32[] limiting_speed
string[] limiting_shape
# Smallest clearances over the segment's moving pieces (m, lower bounds) to any obstacle, to
# obstacles that may move, and to unsafe space (unknown or contaminated shadow).
float32[] clearance_occupied
float32[] clearance_moving
float32[] clearance_unsafe
# The segment sweeps an obstacle (replan), or unsafe space (contact speed, sensitive mode).
bool[] blocked
bool[] unsafe

# Start time of the oldest LiDAR frame behind the answer, and how old it was (s).
builtin_interfaces/Time grid_stamp
float32 grid_age
